cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Crypto-agility for legacy objects: support, references, coverage and transition authority"
message: "Please cite this note and its accompanying diagnostic code. See LICENSE for file-specific terms."
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Khan
    given-names: Arifa
abstract: >-
  A diagnostic framework for migration of existing protected objects. It separates
  mechanism support, authorization-reference mutability, declared population
  coverage and transition authority. The accompanying code checks declared inputs
  and computes the conditional identity R=(1-r)(1-q) using rational arithmetic.
  R denotes all weight not successfully transitioned, including disabled objects
  without restored continuity. It is not an empirical measurement, completeness
  proof or migration mechanism. Primary object continuity alone determines
  neither authorization nor downstream compatibility.
keywords:
  - cryptographic agility
  - post-quantum migration
  - key rotation
  - legacy object migration
